.TH KINTSUGI-RUN 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-run \- run one task to completion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi run
[flags] "<task>"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a single task to completion. The agent reads your codebase, makes changes,
and reports what it did. Output streams to stdout by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-model\fR
Provider/model to use (e.g., ollama/llama3)
.IP \fB\-\-persona\fR
Persona name override
.IP \fB\-\-profile\fR
Behavior profile
.IP \fB\-\-yolo\fR
Skip tool approvals (dangerous)
.IP \fB\-\-frame\fR
Inject Authorization & Domain context
.IP \fB\-\-role\fR
Model role: default|coder|researcher|opsec
.IP \fB\-\-resume\fR
Session id to continue
.IP \fB\-\-output\-format\fR
Output format: text|json|stream-json
.IP \fB\-\-architect\fR
Plan first on architect model, then edit
.IP \fB\-\-architect\-model\fR
Model for architect phase
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a simple task:
.PP
  $ kintsugi run "add error handling to main.go"
.PP
Use a specific model:
.PP
  $ kintsugi run --model ollama/llama3 "fix the bug in auth.go"
.PP
Plan then execute:
.PP
  $ kintsugi run --architect "refactor the database layer"
.PP
Resume a session:
.PP
  $ kintsugi run --resume abc123 "continue where we left off"
.PP
JSON output for scripting:
.PP
  $ kintsugi run --output-format json "list all TODOs" | jq .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-plan (1)
